. Print book; no official copy online.","rd":[["Topics that cite it (Vachanamrut Nondh)","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"desh-vibhag-lekh","g":"Desh Vibhag no Lekh","t":"Desh Vibhag no Lekh","gu":"દેશવિભાગનો લેખ","l":"Gujarati","c":"Life & leela of Shriji","u":null,"m":"scroll","by":"Bhagwan Shri Swaminarayan (written by Shuk Muni)","yr":"Magshar sud 15, V.S. 1883 (1826)","d":"The document by which Shri Hari divided the sampraday into the NarNarayan Dev (Ahmedabad) and LaxmiNarayan Dev (Vadtal) dioceses under the two Acharyas. Kaal Patrak cites it for the day of the division.","rd":[["The day in Kaal Patrak","../kaal-patrak/"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"sksst-timeline","g":"Lord Swaminarayan's Timeline","t":"Lord Swaminarayan's Timeline","gu":"ભગવાન સ્વામિનારાયણ સમયરેખા","l":"English","c":"Life & leela of Shriji","u":"https://cdn.sksst.org/site/documents/bym/topics%20covered/lord_swaminarayans_timeline.pdf","m":"path","pub":"Shree Kutch Satsang Swaminarayan Temple, London (Bhuj, NarNarayan Dev diocese)","d":"A year-by-year timeline of Shri Hari's life from the Bhuj diocese temple in London, used by Kaal Patrak for events no granth dates.","hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"ghanshyam-daily-ritual","g":"Ghanshyam Maharaj's Daily Ritual","t":"Ghanshyam Maharaj's Daily Ritual","gu":"ઘનશ્યામ મહારાજની દૈનિક સેવા","l":"English","c":"Rites, vrat & seva","u":"https://cdn.sksst.org/site/documents/bym/topics%20covered/ghanshyam_maharajs_daily_ritual.pdf","m":"diya","pub":"Shree Kutch Satsang Swaminarayan Temple, London (Bhuj, NarNarayan Dev diocese)","d":"The daily seva of Ghanshyam Maharaj, from mangla to shayan, used on the Shangaar page for the darshan of each part of the day.","hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"samaj-sudharak-en","g":"Samaj Sudharak","t":"Social Reformer Lord Shree Swaminarayan","l":"English","c":"Teachings & commentary","u":null,"m":"book","by":"Dr. Swami Satyaprasaddasji; tr. Ashish Raval","pub":"Shree NarNarayan Dev Sahitya Series no. 42, Bhuj","yr":"2010","d":"The English edition of Samaj Sudharak. Its dates were cross-checked against Shri Swaminarayanam for the Dinacharya. Uploaded copy only; read the Gujarati edition from Bhuj.","hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-veda","g":"The Vedas","t":"The Vedas","gu":"વેદ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"fire","d":"The four Vedas (Ṛg, Yajur, Sāma, Atharva), cited as the highest scriptural authority. Rigveda in full, with recitations, is on the Vedas page. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 44 mentions in 26 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Rigveda reader and recitations","../vedas.html"],["Every citation in the Vachanamrut","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-upanishad","g":"Upanishads","t":"Upanishads","gu":"ઉપનિષદ્","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"om","d":"The philosophical portion of the Vedas. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 7 mentions in 6 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-vedanta","g":"Vedanta and the Vyas Sutras","t":"Vedanta and the Vyas Sutras","gu":"વેદાંત","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"om","d":"The Upaniṣadic philosophy and its sūtras and commentaries (the text mentions Rāmānuja's bhāṣya), together with its critique of \"dry\" Vedāntins (śuṣka-vedānti). The Shikshapatri names the Vyas Sutras with Ramanujacharya's bhashya among the sat-shastras. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 49 mentions in 21 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-sankhya","g":"Sankhya shastra","t":"Sankhya shastra","gu":"સાંખ્ય","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"chakra","d":"The Sāṅkhya system and its texts, one of the four śāstras the text often lists together (Sāṅkhya, Yoga, Vedānta, Pañcarātra). Cited in the Vachanamrut: 63 mentions in 19 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-yoga","g":"Yoga shastra","t":"Yoga shastra","gu":"યોગશાસ્ત્ર","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"lotus","d":"The Yoga system of Patañjali and related texts. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 14 mentions in 7 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-purana","g":"The Puranas","t":"The Puranas","gu":"પુરાણ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"scroll","d":"References to the Purāṇas as a body of scripture. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 40 mentions in 24 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-skanda","g":"Skanda Purana","t":"Skanda Purana","gu":"સ્કંદપુરાણ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"conch","d":"The largest of the Purāṇas. The Vasudev Mahatmya, one of the eight sat-shastras, is part of its Vishnu khand. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 2 mentions in 2 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-padma","g":"Padma Purana","t":"Padma Purana","gu":"પદ્મપુરાણ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"lotus","d":"A Vaiṣṇava Purāṇa. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 2 mentions in 1 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-mahabharata","g":"Mahabharata","t":"Mahabharata","gu":"મહાભારત","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"chakra","d":"The great epic, including the Mokṣadharma and the Udyoga-parva. The Gita, Vidurniti and Vishnu Sahasranam, three of the eight sat-shastras, come from it. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 24 mentions in 21 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-ramayana","g":"Ramayana","t":"Ramayana","gu":"રામાયણ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"bow","d":"Vālmīki's epic of Rāma. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 5 mentions in 3 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-smriti","g":"Smritis and Dharmashastra","t":"Smritis and Dharmashastra","gu":"સ્મૃતિ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"scales","d":"Law books such as the Manu-, Yājñavalkya-, Parāśara- and Śaṅkha-Likhita-smṛtis, and dharmaśāstra in general. \"Smṛti\" is counted only where it means scripture, not remembrance. The Shikshapatri names the Yajnavalkya Smriti among the eight sat-shastras. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 27 mentions in 18 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"shastra-pancharatra","g":"Pancharatra","t":"Pancharatra","gu":"પંચરાત્ર","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Shastras cited in the Vachanamrut","u":"index.html#sources","m":"diya","d":"The Vaiṣṇava ritual and devotional āgamas, including the Nārada Pañcarātra. Cited in the Vachanamrut: 10 mentions in 5 Vachanamruts.","rd":[["Every citation in context","index.html#sources"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"samaveda","g":"Samaveda","t":"Samaveda","gu":"સામવેદ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Veda & Jyotish","u":"https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Sama_Veda","m":"tanpura","d":"The Veda of chant; the Vedas page uses Griffith's translation.","rd":[["Griffith's translation (Wikisource)","https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Sama_Veda"],["On the Vedas page","../vedas.html"]],"hw":false,"v":null,"s":null},{"id":"yajurveda","g":"White Yajurveda","t":"White Yajurveda","gu":"શુક્લ યજુર્વેદ","l":"Sanskrit","c":"Veda & Jyotish